# Emberheart Challenger's valiant counts only spells and abilities ITS CONTROLLER controls. On turn 2 Bot2 casts Lightning
# Bolt at the Challenger (that targeting is not Bot1's and does not use up the "first time"; the checks show only the Bolt
# on the stack and nothing exiled, so it triggered nothing), and Bot1 responds with
# Snakeskin Veil on it: Bot1's first targeting that turn, so valiant triggers and exiles Mox Sapphire from the top of
# Bot1's library. The Veil resolves (+1/+1 counter, hexproof), so the Bolt, whose target is now illegal, does nothing:
# the Challenger lives as a 3/3. "Until end of turn, you may play that card": it is Bot2's turn and an artifact
# cannot be cast then, so the permission ends unused, and on Bot1's turn 3 the Mox Sapphire may not be cast
# (a refusal, with the positive control in emberheart-challenger-valiant-on-a-nonland-card-cast-from-exile-the-same-turn).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Emberheart Challenger
Snakeskin Veil
Island x2
Mox Sapphire
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x5
Island x13

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Emberheart Challenger.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Emberheart Challenger)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
? Stack.Count = 1
? Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Snakeskin Veil.Cast(Emberheart Challenger)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Exile = Mox Sapphire
! Bot1.Exile.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile = Mox Sapphire
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Ruby; Mox Jet; Mox Emerald; Emberheart Challenger
Bot1.Battlefield.Emberheart Challenger.Power = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Emberheart Challenger.Toughness = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Emberheart Challenger.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Graveyard = Snakeskin Veil
